<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jerez de la Frontera</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jerez de la Frontera is a city in the province of Cádiz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalete">Guadalete</a> river. Under Muslim rule it was the town of Sharish, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> conquered it in the 13th century, after which it lay on the frontier with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. It is famous as the home of sherry wine, named after the town, and for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-breeding">horse breeding</a> and flamenco.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jerez-de-la-frontera.jpg" alt="Jerez de la Frontera" width="320" height="116" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Annie and Andrew · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Jerez_de_la_Frontera)_DSC_0560_(6271831479)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
